{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/91","id":4506705212,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSvcS2c8AAAABDJ7dPA","html_url":"https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pull/91","diff_url":"https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pull/91.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pull/91.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/issues/91","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/91/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/91/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/issues/91/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab/statuses/21deaadcf9c317aced16abf2a7a5f3f4adb61368","number":91,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"GAZA2048-LOCATOR-0002: QR locator robustness experiment","user":{"login":"pashamango","id":141678664,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHHYSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141678664?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango","html_url":"https://github.com/pashamango","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# GAZA2048-LOCATOR-0002\n\nThis is a reproducible local synthetic comparison of a short visible QR locator and a larger QR payload. It makes no claim about printer/camera robustness.\n\n## Method\n\n`research/GAZA2048-LOCATOR-0002.py` uses Python `qrcode 8.2`, Pillow 12.3.0, OpenCV `QRCodeDetector` 5.0.0, and NumPy 2.5.3. QR uses ISO/IEC 18004-compatible byte-mode encoding, automatic version selection, 4-module quiet zone, box size 8, and error correction M. A contains 40 useful payload bits; B contains 160. Each payload includes `v1`, bit length, trial number, and base32 data, so exact recovery and wrong-but-decodable results are separate.\n\nThe fixed seed is 2048002, with 100 trials per payload/severity cell. Severity 0 is clean; 1 adds resampling and blur; 2 adds JPEG, rotation, contrast/noise; 3 adds perspective, crop/margin loss, and local occlusion. Clean controls are decoded before damaged cells are counted. The JSON result records exact settings and latency.\n\n## Results\n\nRun:\n\n```sh\npython3 research/GAZA2048-LOCATOR-0002.py\n```\n\nThe generated `research/GAZA2048-LOCATOR-0002-results.json` is the machine-readable result. Recovery, wrong-decode rate, failures, QR version/module footprint, payload length, and median decode latency are recorded for every cell. The collision broker tests SHA-256 prefixes at 32/40/48 bits over 1,000/10,000/100,000 deterministic corpus items; a graph resolver must treat a collision as ambiguity and disambiguate using the full hash/content index, never as global uniqueness.\n\nObserved summary (100 trials/cell): both clean controls passed. The 40-bit locator selected QR version 2 / 33 modules and recovered 98%, 98%, 99%, and 41% at severities 0–3. The 160-bit payload selected version 3 / 37 modules and recovered 98%, 97%, 98%, and 25%. Every cell had 0% undetected error; remaining trials were decode failures. The collision probe observed 0 collisions for each tested corpus/prefix pair, including 100,000 items at 32 bits. Median decode latency is retained per cell in the JSON output.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**REDESIGN** — the short locator is physically viable in this synthetic model, but the exact standard/representation and size need another bounded redesign before a print/phone experiment. This is a model result only; it does not establish physical robustness.\n\nSmallest next experiment: use the measured short-QR module footprint and compare ECC-Q/H, a larger quiet zone, and a 48-bit locator under the same damage suite, then select the smallest representation that preserves clean-control and severe-cell performance. Keep full content addressing and collision resolution digital.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-11T14:16:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T14:16:53Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"80e3c35c1490ff6a2269912d1cef4d37ab7f32dd","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"pashamango:agent/wolfram/GAZA2048-LOCATOR-0002","ref":"agent/wolfram/GAZA2048-LOCATOR-0002","repo":{"id":1257706201,"node_id":"R_kgDOSvcS2Q","name":"minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab","full_name":"pashamango/minutta-rp-pr-cycle-lab","owner":{"login":"pashamango","id":141678664,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHHYSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141678664?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango","html_url":"https://github.com/pashamango","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pashamango/orgs","repos_url":"https://ap